From 70fbfbb388daa9ac4d044e1b974d6d0c2a6b8cd4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 11:22:42 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] rc, www: hardware QoS never shapes a WAN VLAN's parent that
 also carries the LAN (field, GT-BE98 family)

v3.3.7 made hwqos_tm_ifname() resolve an 802.1Q WAN device to its parent so a
PPPoE line is shaped on its physical port. On the boards with the external 2.5G
switch (GT-BE98, GT-BE98 Pro, GT-BE96, GT-BE19000) the "2.5G WAN/LAN-1" jack is
vlan4094 on eth1, and eth1 is also LAN-2..4 and a wired AiMesh backhaul. With
hardware QoS on, the whole classful program (queues deleted and recreated, PI2,
the shapers, the port shaper at the upload rate, the policer) landed on the LAN
trunk: the wired LAN and the backhaul throttled to the upload rate, the main
router at load 17 with ksoftirqd and bcmsw_rx burning, 45 of 2400 flows
accelerated, eight daemons stuck on rtnl_lock, a wired node unable to rejoin.
Three GT-BE98 Pro units on v3.3.8, diag v1.3.33 (WAN vlan4094, qos_type 11,
eth1 in br0). v3.3.6 pointed tmctl at vlan4094 itself, which it refuses
(rc=108), so hardware QoS on that jack was inert and nobody noticed.

A resolved parent that is a bridge member (/sys/class/net/<if>/brport) or is
listed in lan_ifnames is never shaped: hwqos_tm_ifname() returns no port, both
engines refuse to arm and log why, and the QoS page shows RQOS_125 next to the
engine choice when wan0_ifname is a vlanNNNN device. A PPPoE VLAN on a dedicated
WAN port still resolves to its parent (v3.3.7 kept). Host tests
test_hwqos_lan_trunk.py, test_hwqos_pppoe.py (harness extended); markers pin
the staged rc and page.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
